title: Single source of truth for builtin method surfaces
status: complete
atomic: false
priority: high
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-04T04:27:12'
updated_at: '2026-06-04T05:15:08'
result: 'Introduced src/builtin_methods.rs as the single shared registry of builtin
  Vec/Map/String method surfaces (VecMethod/MapMethod/StrMethod enums with from_name
  + ret_ty). The typer (string/vec/map_method_ret_ty, is_string_exclusive_method in
  src/typer/mod.rs) now delegates entirely to it. Codegen (src/codegen/mir_codegen/emit_inst/core.rs)
  resolves the method name to the registry enum and matches it EXHAUSTIVELY, so adding
  a variant in the registry breaks the codegen build until an arm is wired — making
  typer/codegen drift impossible. This surfaced and fixed 6 latent drift bugs that
  typechecked but failed codegen with "unknown method": Vec.chain, Vec.flatten, Vec.enumerate,
  Map.keys, Map.values (now implemented: vec_chain_v/vec_enumerate_v/vec_flatten_v
  in transforms.rs, map_keys/map_values in map.rs), plus removed the never-implemented
  String.matches/find_all/replace_re from the surface (regex lives in std.regex).
  Added tests/builtin_method_surface.rs conformance (6 tests) pinning the runtime
  behaviour. Full suite green: 1639 passed, 0 failed; zero build warnings; clippy
  clean.'
description: 'The Vec/Map/String builtin method tables consulted by the typer and
  codegen must be the same table, so typer/codegen drift (the shift/first/last bug)
  becomes impossible. Introduce a shared enum BuiltinMethod (or shared descriptor
  table) that both passes match on exhaustively, or make codegen-completeness a compile-time-checked
  exhaustiveness over the typer''s set. Definition of done: a single shared registry
  of builtin methods (name, receiver type, signature) referenced by both typer and
  codegen; adding a method in one place forces the other; tests still green.'
